            <div xml:id="d498">

                <pb facs="0692" n="568" sameAs="frus:frus1923v02/pg568"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.24/197: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Guatemala</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Geissler</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-12-28T12:00:00-07:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 28,
                                1923—12 noon</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received 8 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>101. Acting general manager International Railways informs me that his New York
                    office has authorized him to sell Mexican Government <pb facs="0693" n="569"
                        xml:id="pg569"/> 1,000 barrels of oil per week at Ayutla if there is no
                    objection made by the Government of Guatemala or the American Minister. Please
                    instruct me by cable.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Geissler</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
